>>
Rule 1 (valid tensor input is provided)
{v_1 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (when out is provided, it must be a Tensor and match the input shape)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= ndim(v_1) = ndim(v_2) ∧ ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
>>
Rule 3 (out dtype must be compatible with the result; enforce by matching input dtype to suppress cast errors)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= dtype_(v_2) = dtype_(v_1)
>>
Rule 4 (scalar handling: scalar input implies scalar out; otherwise per-dimension equality)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if ndim(v_1) = 0 then ndim(v_2) = 0 else ∀i ∈ [0, ndim(v_1) - 1] : shape(v_1, i) = shape(v_2, i)
